1
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:04,800
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:10,610
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:14,550
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:17,390
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,790 --> 00:00:21,520
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:52,890 --> 00:00:54,720
What is this?

7
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:00,030
Why?

8
00:01:00,470 --> 00:01:03,300
Why are we here?

9
00:01:24,430 --> 00:01:26,520
Feel no shame about shape

10
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:28,440
Weather changes their phrase

11
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:32,190
Even mother will show you another way

12
00:01:32,190 --> 00:01:34,570
So put your glasses on

13
00:01:34,650 --> 00:01:36,650
Nothing will be wrong

14
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:38,860
There's no blame. There's no fame

15
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:40,700
It's up to you

16
00:01:40,870 --> 00:01:44,330
The first words should be found

17
00:01:44,950 --> 00:01:47,960
Whatever holds you back

18
00:01:48,830 --> 00:01:49,330
I...

19
00:01:49,710 --> 00:01:50,460
...can...

20
00:01:50,540 --> 00:01:52,630
I can get it off

21
00:01:52,630 --> 00:01:53,630
Tell me what...

22
00:01:53,630 --> 00:01:54,630
Tell me what...

23
00:01:54,630 --> 00:01:56,470
Tell me what you want

24
00:01:56,590 --> 00:01:57,550
I don't know why...

25
00:01:57,760 --> 00:01:58,550
Don't know why...

26
00:01:58,550 --> 00:02:00,550
Don't know why you're afraid

27
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:01,720
Tell me what...

28
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:02,680
Tell me what...

29
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:04,350
Tell me what you'd say

30
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:05,680
I don't know why...

31
00:02:05,810 --> 00:02:06,770
Don't know why...

32
00:02:06,850 --> 00:02:07,560
Too late...

33
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:09,190
It's too late

34
00:02:14,110 --> 00:02:18,110
Time of Eternity

35
00:02:23,870 --> 00:02:26,370
The symbol that has
been branded on to your skin...

36
00:02:26,450 --> 00:02:27,960
...marks you as sacrificial offerings.

37
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:31,040
The lives of those
who have been branded now...

38
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:35,090
...belong to us as offerings.
Every last drop of your blood...

39
00:02:35,590 --> 00:02:37,170
...until your dying gasps...

40
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:40,510
...is food for the life of our
beloved unborn child of darkness.

41
00:02:41,220 --> 00:02:42,220
Wait!

42
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:44,560
Hang on, Griffith!

43
00:02:45,390 --> 00:02:48,230
I'll get you out of there soon!

44
00:02:48,930 --> 00:02:50,100
It's no use!

45
00:02:50,190 --> 00:02:52,770
Human strength is utterly
useless in this situation.

46
00:02:53,020 --> 00:02:56,150
Your efforts are futile in this matter.

47
00:02:56,230 --> 00:02:58,400
All is dictated by his own will.

48
00:02:58,650 --> 00:02:59,570
Shut up!

49
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:02,110
You must have heard what we said...

50
00:03:02,490 --> 00:03:04,240
He's the one who has the final word.

51
00:03:04,450 --> 00:03:05,580
I said...

52
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:06,830
Shut up!

53
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:13,420
That's not possible!

54
00:03:35,110 --> 00:03:36,110
Was it you...

55
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:38,780
Was it you who wanted this?

56
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:52,250
Sacrifice, sacrifice, sacrifice...

57
00:04:22,490 --> 00:04:23,320
Pippin!

58
00:04:23,610 --> 00:04:24,490
Run!

59
00:04:28,080 --> 00:04:28,780
Go!

60
00:04:29,030 --> 00:04:30,330
Run! Run away!

61
00:04:30,450 --> 00:04:31,950
You must survive!

62
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:33,410
What are you saying?

63
00:04:36,670 --> 00:04:37,790
What are you doing?

64
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:39,210
Let go! Pippin is...

65
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:45,590
Pippin!

66
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:47,850
We can't leave him there to die!

67
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:49,100
Stop it!

68
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:51,930
You are our leader now!

69
00:04:52,270 --> 00:04:53,480
You must survive!

70
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:56,150
If our commander's alive,
it's not over for the Band of the Hawk!

71
00:04:56,520 --> 00:05:00,770
Not like this!
I won't let it be over... Not like this!

72
00:05:19,710 --> 00:05:22,000
Commander!

73
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:05,920
A dream.

74
00:06:06,550 --> 00:06:08,880
This is all a dream!

75
00:06:10,550 --> 00:06:11,850
The Midland army...

76
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:13,680
The Band of the Hawk...

77
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:15,850
It was all a dream!

78
00:06:16,810 --> 00:06:22,480
If you think about it,
it was all too good to be true...

79
00:06:23,020 --> 00:06:25,530
That's right!

80
00:06:25,650 --> 00:06:27,360
All a dream!

81
00:06:28,150 --> 00:06:30,950
This is all a dream!

82
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:33,870
When I open my eyes,
everything will be over!

83
00:06:46,510 --> 00:06:47,460
It'll just be me.

84
00:06:47,670 --> 00:06:49,630
A woman in hell?

85
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:51,550
This must be a dream.

86
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:55,060
Damn it.

87
00:06:55,510 --> 00:06:57,680
I'm such a sucker.

88
00:06:58,230 --> 00:07:00,190
Why?

89
00:07:03,770 --> 00:07:05,110
Damn it.

90
00:07:15,950 --> 00:07:17,160
Judeau, to your right!

91
00:07:21,370 --> 00:07:22,170
Judeau!

92
00:07:26,550 --> 00:07:27,500
Are you all right?

93
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:30,470
Yeah, you saved me.

94
00:07:32,510 --> 00:07:33,390
Judeau...

95
00:07:35,050 --> 00:07:36,140
That's enough...

96
00:07:36,220 --> 00:07:37,180
Turn back!

97
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:39,310
It's the same wherever we go!

98
00:07:39,350 --> 00:07:40,680
They'll come after us!

99
00:07:41,690 --> 00:07:45,610
We should at least go down together
with our swords in our hands.

100
00:07:45,940 --> 00:07:47,730
Quiet, you'll bite your tongue!

101
00:07:48,820 --> 00:07:50,190
We've got to struggle through it.

102
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:54,110
We have to keep struggling
right to the bitter end.

103
00:07:55,320 --> 00:07:57,990
I'll be damned if we go back
to face them just to get killed.

104
00:07:58,830 --> 00:08:00,700
No thanks, I don't want that.

105
00:08:00,750 --> 00:08:01,870
Guts wouldn't either.

106
00:08:09,590 --> 00:08:10,460
Judeau!

107
00:08:19,310 --> 00:08:20,140
Judeau!

108
00:08:23,730 --> 00:08:25,230
You fool! Get out of the way!

109
00:08:28,900 --> 00:08:29,940
Why are you...

110
00:08:30,860 --> 00:08:31,940
That's enough.

111
00:08:32,530 --> 00:08:34,030
Stop!

112
00:08:55,260 --> 00:08:56,050
Judeau!

113
00:08:57,050 --> 00:08:58,350
Did I get him?

114
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:01,270
With my last knife?

115
00:09:01,350 --> 00:09:02,720
Yes, you got him.

116
00:09:02,770 --> 00:09:03,640
He's dead.

117
00:09:04,940 --> 00:09:05,940
Go...

118
00:09:06,230 --> 00:09:07,650
What the hell are you saying?

119
00:09:07,730 --> 00:09:10,940
You just said we have to struggle
and struggle until the very end!

120
00:09:11,150 --> 00:09:12,070
Stand up!

121
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:14,400
I'm taking you with me,
even if I have to drag you!

122
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:17,820
All right...

123
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:19,780
I'll accompany you.

124
00:09:19,870 --> 00:09:21,290
Even if it means I have to crawl...

125
00:09:21,330 --> 00:09:23,500
Yes, you'd better!

126
00:09:23,950 --> 00:09:26,830
I guess I wasn't in my right
mind when I said all that.

127
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:29,420
Take responsibility for your own words.

128
00:09:29,630 --> 00:09:32,250
I'm afraid I've always been,
you know, all talk.

129
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:34,340
If you have the strength for excuses...

130
00:09:34,460 --> 00:09:36,090
...use it to walk!

131
00:09:36,380 --> 00:09:40,510
I always thought I was
at least pretty articulate...

132
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:42,760
...but it looks like I missed my chance...

133
00:09:44,310 --> 00:09:46,270
Those crucial words...

134
00:09:49,060 --> 00:09:52,520
You sure do cry a lot, don't you?

135
00:09:54,070 --> 00:09:57,950
And those are my last words...

136
00:10:04,370 --> 00:10:05,370
Judeau?

137
00:10:43,370 --> 00:10:44,330
The living sacrifice...

138
00:10:44,370 --> 00:10:45,910
Living sacrifice...

139
00:10:46,040 --> 00:10:47,660
The sacrificial woman...

140
00:10:49,210 --> 00:10:50,960
The sacrificial woman...

141
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:54,420
Shall we eat?

142
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:56,380
Shall we eat now?

143
00:10:57,050 --> 00:10:59,380
But before that...

144
00:10:59,760 --> 00:11:01,720
Before that...

145
00:11:02,590 --> 00:11:03,600
Guts!

146
00:11:29,580 --> 00:11:31,750
That boy really does try hard, doesn't he?

147
00:11:35,750 --> 00:11:37,130
Isn't it ironic?

148
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:40,340
The more powerful his vitality is...

149
00:11:40,670 --> 00:11:43,640
...and the longer
he draws out this struggle...

150
00:11:44,090 --> 00:11:48,310
...the more precious he will be for the
new life to feed on in the darkness.

151
00:11:48,970 --> 00:11:51,230
Sweet dreams, our newborn Apostle.

152
00:11:53,310 --> 00:11:56,150
Your entire being is built upon Griffith's dream.

153
00:11:58,480 --> 00:12:00,490
When Griffith's dream dies with him...

154
00:12:00,570 --> 00:12:02,610
...you will finally open your eyes...

155
00:12:03,110 --> 00:12:05,740
...and be brought to life
in your own never-ending dream.

156
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:14,790
Where...

157
00:12:16,040 --> 00:12:17,500
Where am I?

158
00:12:18,710 --> 00:12:20,210
I feel my body...

159
00:12:21,510 --> 00:12:23,010
...sinking...

160
00:12:24,550 --> 00:12:25,680
...deep...

161
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:03,760
Their deaths pierce through me.

162
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:08,300
The men I killed...

163
00:13:09,430 --> 00:13:11,060
Because of my desires...

164
00:13:12,430 --> 00:13:13,600
How strange...

165
00:13:14,180 --> 00:13:15,560
I don't feel a thing...

166
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,060
I'm just sinking...

167
00:13:24,950 --> 00:13:26,070
What's this?

168
00:13:26,610 --> 00:13:30,370
The last tear you shed.

169
00:13:34,750 --> 00:13:39,580
When a person suffers so much
that he is almost torn in two...

170
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:41,670
...his heart freezes.

171
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:46,930
Behelits?

172
00:13:47,510 --> 00:13:49,550
These are just splashes...

173
00:13:50,300 --> 00:13:53,640
Splashes spilling
from one ocean to another.

174
00:13:53,850 --> 00:13:55,850
A droplet of the future...

175
00:13:56,350 --> 00:13:58,600
Summoning you from the other world...

176
00:14:31,050 --> 00:14:31,970
Blood!

177
00:14:41,350 --> 00:14:43,150
Isn't anyone alive?

178
00:14:43,730 --> 00:14:44,570
Judeau!

179
00:14:44,940 --> 00:14:45,860
Pippin!

180
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:47,440
Corkus!

181
00:14:49,990 --> 00:14:51,490
Casca...

182
00:14:52,660 --> 00:14:53,950
Commander...

183
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:58,120
Gaston!

184
00:14:58,500 --> 00:14:59,870
You're alive!

185
00:15:02,670 --> 00:15:05,590
Well, I hardly feel like I'm alive anymore.

186
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:07,460
Where's the rest of the group?

187
00:15:07,550 --> 00:15:08,800
Who else is alive?

188
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:10,680
I don't know.

189
00:15:10,970 --> 00:15:13,390
I was running like hell trying to get away.

190
00:15:14,010 --> 00:15:16,510
Next thing I knew, I found myself like this.

191
00:15:17,060 --> 00:15:20,350
I don't know
what happened to the rest of them.

192
00:15:22,020 --> 00:15:23,310
Commander.

193
00:15:23,810 --> 00:15:25,770
What do you think this means?

194
00:15:26,520 --> 00:15:28,940
It's as if we're in a bad dream.

195
00:15:31,780 --> 00:15:32,410
Gaston!

196
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:48,800
Pippin!

197
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:50,590
You're alive!

198
00:15:51,590 --> 00:15:52,510
Pippin!

199
00:16:31,550 --> 00:16:33,760
You bastards!

200
00:16:35,430 --> 00:16:37,800
You bastards!

201
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:37,860
It is the birth...

202
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:40,160
...of our fifth blessed ruler...

203
00:17:40,240 --> 00:17:42,700
Our new demon king...

204
00:17:43,750 --> 00:17:45,620
You are one of us...

205
00:17:45,710 --> 00:17:49,130
Our latest kin to wear the crown of evil.

206
00:17:50,130 --> 00:17:52,170
The Wings of Darkness...

207
00:17:52,250 --> 00:17:53,510
Femto!

208
00:18:23,660 --> 00:18:25,500
Griffith?

209
00:18:54,230 --> 00:18:55,610
Griffith?

210
00:19:53,710 --> 00:19:55,170
Griffith!

211
00:20:16,690 --> 00:20:18,150
Oh, it's beautiful...

212
00:20:18,230 --> 00:20:19,940
How it moves me...

213
00:20:21,190 --> 00:20:25,620
Love, hatred, torment, pleasure...

214
00:20:25,780 --> 00:20:27,660
Life and death...

215
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:30,200
All at once before our eyes...

216
00:20:30,500 --> 00:20:32,210
This is the beauty of man...

217
00:20:32,500 --> 00:20:34,170
...and evil.

218
00:21:21,340 --> 00:21:23,800
Looking back, the morning comes.

219
00:21:23,800 --> 00:21:27,300
Don't find your face in your glass.

220
00:21:28,340 --> 00:21:31,430
Take the moonlight by the tail.

221
00:21:31,430 --> 00:21:34,390
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

222
00:21:35,850 --> 00:21:37,600
What is that?

223
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:38,860
It's just the same.

224
00:21:38,860 --> 00:21:42,030
What is trying your crown?

225
00:21:43,110 --> 00:21:46,320
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

226
00:21:46,320 --> 00:21:49,370
So wear my glass. You're fading.

227
00:21:49,660 --> 00:22:09,260
I'm waiting so long.

228
00:22:09,260 --> 00:22:18,350
I'm waiting...

229
00:22:39,210 --> 00:22:40,540
You going?

230
00:22:42,920 --> 00:22:44,840
Don't get yourself killed.

